"patch":"@@ -30,4 +30,4 @@ If you could only use other machines (for example the Iris practice cluster or a\n \n Show the common baseline for your platform alongside your result, in whatever form suits your slides: a sentence, a row in your results table, a reference line or bar in a chart. Only the number and its source need to be clear. One way to write it: \"4-node 2.03 s/step; common baseline (vanilla `scotch`, Gadi) 2.126 s/step (−4.5%)\".\n \n-Keep your own baseline as well: it shows your path, and Bonus work is still measured against your own Basic result (README R3). If your own untuned run on the same platform differs from the common baseline, keep it as your own baseline and show both. This only asks for one more line in your slides, not for new runs.\n+This only asks for one more line in your slides, not for new runs. Bonus work is still measured against your own Basic result (README R3)."}]}